# Translations (i18next)

## Setup

- Config: `src/i18n/index.ts`
- Locale files: `src/locales/{en,hi,ta,te,kn,ml,mr,gu}.ts`
- Each locale exports a flat nested object — **en.ts** is the source of truth

## Using Translations

```tsx
const { t } = useTranslation();
t('home.attendanceManagement.mark.title')
t('modals.timePicker.rangeError', { min: '9:00 AM', max: '6:00 PM' }) // interpolation
```

## Key Naming Convention

Hierarchical, dot-separated, matching feature area:

```
home.attendanceManagement.title          // screen title
home.attendanceManagement.mark.statuses.present  // nested feature
modals.timePicker.am                     // modal-level
settings.alerts.ok                       // settings area
```

## Adding New Keys

1. Add keys to `src/locales/en.ts` first (English is the base)
2. Add matching keys to other locale files when translations are available
3. Group under the feature namespace (e.g., `home.attendanceManagement.bulk.*`)
4. Use interpolation `{{var}}` for dynamic values, not string concatenation
